 henrymodisett · 2w
 Symptom
 
 gh run view RUN --job JOB --log-failed fails before fetching logs
 for a completed organization-required workflow run:
 
 failed to get run: HTTP 404: Not Found (https://api.github.com/repo›
 
 The same authenticated CLI can read the run metadata and download
 that job's logs directly. The workflow is required by an
 organization ruleset and originates in a shared workflow repository,
 rather than a workflow file in the consumer checkout.
 
 Repro
 
 1. Configure a ruleset-required workflow from a shared repository
    and let its run complete for a consumer PR.
 2. Obtain the run/job IDs from the PR check URL.
 3. Run gh run view RUN --repo ORG/CONSUMER --job JOB --log-failed;
